WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.780
In Souls we talk a lot about disparity

00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:06.509
about what lies between light and dark

00:00:06.509 --> 00:00:10.200
life and death, heat and cold and today

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:13.180
we discuss two different absolutes.

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:15.870
We discuss what lies between those with

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:17.650
power and those without.

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:19.560
And in this case,

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:22.300
what lies between them is a wall.

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:25.199
A stone wall that appeared quite suddenly

00:00:25.199 --> 00:00:28.320
cementing this divide between hollows

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:30.400
and the nobles who control them

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:32.220
and mind you

00:00:32.620 --> 00:00:34.820
wall or not there has always been a

00:00:34.829 --> 00:00:37.770
divide. In the days of Lordran humanity

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:40.590
was a rising force and as a result they

00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:43.230
were feared imprisoned and shepherded

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:45.750
they were taught to fear the undead

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:46.900
rising in their ranks.

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:48.720
In Drangleic the

00:00:48.899 --> 00:00:51.300
undead were subjugated once more

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:52.739
of course, but they were also

00:00:52.739 --> 00:00:56.010
experimented upon and all the while they

00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:58.949
were expected to sacrifice themselves as

00:00:58.949 --> 00:01:03.009
Gwyn once did, to keep those Royals in power.

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:06.180
And now in Lothric the unkindled

00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:08.729
born of the ash of these unending

00:01:08.729 --> 00:01:12.330
sacrifices, journeys through a small town

00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:13.760
of suffering undead.

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:15.860
It was here where a

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:18.960
thief once fancied himself a martyr for

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:20.200
the poor.

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:22.740
It was the state of this town that drove

00:01:22.750 --> 00:01:24.770
Greirat to climb the wall

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:25.580
[Greirat]

00:01:25.580 --> 00:01:30.260
"Greirat the thief was a some well-known name...

00:01:32.620 --> 00:01:35.440
Until I ended up rotting in a cell..."

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:36.200
[Vaati]

00:01:36.260 --> 00:01:38.920
the head covering he wears was once used to cover

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:41.439
the heads of the lesser folk people who

00:01:41.439 --> 00:01:43.600
were said to work as slaves throughout

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:46.840
Lothric but occasionally it was used to

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:49.640
shame and humiliate criminals.

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:52.260
We have reason to believe that Greirat was

00:01:52.270 --> 00:01:55.599
indeed a slave to the kingdom, once

00:01:55.599 --> 00:01:58.159
for he knows the castle grounds well.

00:01:58.160 --> 00:02:01.500
But here in lower Lothric, Greirat is caught and

00:02:01.509 --> 00:02:04.129
imprisoned for the very first time.

00:02:04.129 --> 00:02:04.620
[Greirat]

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:08.220
"Ah, you are no jailer, are you?"

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:11.680
"No. No, you are from far away."

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:16.840
"Judging by the bell, you must be some of

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:18.940
"that Unkindled Ash."

00:02:19.720 --> 00:02:21.720
"Remarkable"

00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:26.760
"If that's true, then I have a favor to ask."

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:30.600
"Below the high wall is a musty

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:33.660
"little town, not the home of any Lord"

00:02:33.660 --> 00:02:36.750
"just a very old settlement of Undead."

00:02:37.700 --> 00:02:41.420
"An old woman Loretta lives there."

00:02:41.430 --> 00:02:45.070
"Please, give her this ring?"

00:02:45.990 --> 00:02:48.930
"I-I'm not asking for charity, in f-in fact,

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:51.420
"if you do this for me I'll be sure to

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:55.500
"repay you in kind and I may be a petty

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:59.300
"thief but I've got more wits that most royalty."

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:03.880
"What do you say then, hmm?"

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:06.080
"Very well."

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:10.960
"I humbly place my faith in you. I am Greirat,

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:14.700
"of the Undead Settlement, and I

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:16.760
"promise to assist you."

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:19.080
"Give this ring to

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:22.100
"Loretta at the base of the highwall."

00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:26.060
"Do your part and I'll do mine."

00:03:26.070 --> 00:03:26.830
[Vaati]

00:03:26.830 --> 00:03:29.940
We can't know who Loretta was. We don't

00:03:29.970 --> 00:03:33.120
know why her corpse clutches a bone nor

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:35.670
do we know what Greirat's relationship to

00:03:35.670 --> 00:03:39.150
her was, the one detail we do know is

00:03:39.150 --> 00:03:42.090
that the little rare ring he gives us to

00:03:42.090 --> 00:03:45.000
give to her is a tear stone, which has

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:47.820
the uncanny ability to sense imminent

00:03:47.820 --> 00:03:50.880
death protecting its wearer in their

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:54.630
final moments, so whoever she was to him

00:03:54.630 --> 00:03:58.140
it seems he cared for her and sensed her

00:03:58.140 --> 00:03:59.320
death was close.

00:03:59.320 --> 00:04:00.080
[Greirat]

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:02.740
"Heavens! she was already dead?"

00:04:02.940 --> 00:04:04.930
"Thank you."

00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:07.320
"I'm not surprised though..."

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:11.060
"Almost relieved, really."

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:14.520
"You can keep the ring."

00:04:15.160 --> 00:04:15.860
"As..."

00:04:16.920 --> 00:04:17.620
"Well..."

00:04:17.980 --> 00:04:22.600
"A little trinket of thanks I suppose."

00:04:22.600 --> 00:04:23.800
[Vaati]

00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:25.720
He breaks his composure when you appear

00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:29.050
back and from then on dedicates himself

00:04:29.050 --> 00:04:31.390
fully to your cause.

00:04:31.390 --> 00:04:32.090
[Greirat]

00:04:32.090 --> 00:04:34.090
"Ah, there you are."

00:04:34.480 --> 00:04:36.340
"I was thinking..."

00:04:37.660 --> 00:04:39.580
"You know I'm a petty thief,

00:04:39.580 --> 00:04:43.600
"well, perhaps I'll go on the prowl."

00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:45.910
"Everyone's dead or hollowed away anyway,

00:04:45.910 --> 00:04:48.330
"right? So i might as well fetch some

00:04:48.340 --> 00:04:50.440
"weapons or treasure for you."

00:04:51.640 --> 00:04:53.680
"Well, what do you think?"

00:04:55.760 --> 00:04:59.920
"Thank you. You will not be disappointed.

00:05:00.880 --> 00:05:02.560
"I will leave for some time."

00:05:03.480 --> 00:05:05.280
"So long for now."

00:05:05.720 --> 00:05:07.480
"Do stay safe, you hear?"

00:05:07.480 --> 00:05:10.440
"Or my efforts will have been for naught."

00:05:10.440 --> 00:05:11.640
[Vaati]

00:05:11.640 --> 00:05:13.640
Don't take Greirat's robbery of the

00:05:13.740 --> 00:05:16.560
undead settlement lightly, it was his

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:19.470
home. It was the poor there who inspired

00:05:19.480 --> 00:05:21.520
him to climb the wall and risked his

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:24.130
life and it was the settlement where he

00:05:24.130 --> 00:05:27.130
cared deeply for someone. His thievery of

00:05:27.130 --> 00:05:30.050
the settlement is kind of an admission

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:32.840
that everyone there, no longer matters to him

00:05:33.440 --> 00:05:33.940
you do

00:05:34.380 --> 00:05:36.780
and so emboldened by his

00:05:36.780 --> 00:05:39.670
new purpose he asks to put himself in

00:05:39.670 --> 00:05:41.620
harm's way once again

00:05:41.620 --> 00:05:45.560
(Greirat) "oh hello fine work i'd say

00:05:46.260 --> 00:05:49.920
discovering Irithyll in the Boreal Valley all in a

00:05:49.930 --> 00:05:51.410
day's work

00:05:52.560 --> 00:05:54.720
if the tales are true it is

00:05:54.730 --> 00:05:57.930
home to old moon-worshipping nobles

00:05:58.040 --> 00:05:59.840
and should be packed with treasure

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:02.080
what do you think?"

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:05.820
"Shall I go and see what i can find?"

00:06:06.540 --> 00:06:08.180
"mmmm a fine choice

00:06:09.140 --> 00:06:13.319
i am Greirat the thief, what I bring back will be

00:06:13.319 --> 00:06:14.740
worthy of that name"

00:06:17.020 --> 00:06:18.400
(Vaati) that name is also

00:06:18.449 --> 00:06:20.089
known by others

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:22.700
(Patches) "Ahh, I see you've met Greirat.

00:06:23.279 --> 00:06:25.439
The slinking rodent. but he did me a good

00:06:25.439 --> 00:06:27.519
turn back in Lothric dungeon

00:06:27.880 --> 00:06:29.999
Doubtless I should do something about that little

00:06:29.999 --> 00:06:30.689
debt...

00:06:30.689 --> 00:06:34.529
well maybe not, well probably believe

00:06:34.529 --> 00:06:36.969
he's still standing"

00:06:37.440 --> 00:06:42.160
(Vaati) this is Patches, the hyena, the spider, the unbreakable

00:06:42.200 --> 00:06:44.639
by now we have a pretty good grasp of his

00:06:44.639 --> 00:06:47.219
character and it's the same character

00:06:47.219 --> 00:06:50.399
who for the first time expresses a

00:06:50.399 --> 00:06:53.519
genuine concern about the well-being of

00:06:53.519 --> 00:06:54.019
another

00:06:54.460 --> 00:06:57.680
(Patches) "hey what happened to Greirat anyhow?

00:06:57.760 --> 00:07:00.340
I haven't seen him at all lately

00:07:00.380 --> 00:07:02.140
if you know where he's scurried off to

00:07:02.300 --> 00:07:03.660
be sure and tell me

00:07:04.540 --> 00:07:07.540
I need to stock up, and if he's gone and croaked

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:09.920
he'll have left a goldmine.

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:16.480
right yes

00:07:16.490 --> 00:07:20.690
I see how it is.. some things can't be divulged

00:07:20.690 --> 00:07:22.830
even between friends

00:07:22.830 --> 00:07:24.520
that comes with the territory

00:07:24.530 --> 00:07:27.740
fine but if you happen to recall any

00:07:27.740 --> 00:07:31.640
details, do be a saint, do it for old

00:07:31.640 --> 00:07:34.190
Patches Boutique of Wonders at least.. Aye?"

00:07:36.260 --> 00:07:39.320
(Vaati) if Patches is still alive to tell you this

00:07:39.320 --> 00:07:41.840
then it means you've forgiven him for a

00:07:41.840 --> 00:07:44.240
great deal of things you've forgiven him

00:07:44.240 --> 00:07:47.090
for impersonating The Onion Knight, for

00:07:47.090 --> 00:07:49.790
locking you in a tower; he's tried to

00:07:49.790 --> 00:07:52.610
kill you twice now probably and it's

00:07:52.610 --> 00:07:54.590
understandable right that you wouldn't

00:07:54.590 --> 00:07:56.780
want to tell him where your friend is

00:07:56.780 --> 00:07:57.710
gone

00:07:57.710 --> 00:08:00.950
however Greirat can be saved by the

00:08:00.950 --> 00:08:03.790
very thief you tried to protect him from...

00:08:04.140 --> 00:08:06.640
(Patches) "well happen to recall anything important?

00:08:07.240 --> 00:08:11.460
About where that old rat scurried off to.

00:08:12.340 --> 00:08:15.440
What? Gone all the way to Irithyll, has he?

00:08:15.640 --> 00:08:18.600
Well, there can't be much left of that frozen sprawl

00:08:18.920 --> 00:08:23.200
The old rat, he's gone off the deep end this time..."

00:08:23.210 --> 00:08:25.850
(Vaati) was Greirat truly saved by Sigward here?

00:08:26.200 --> 00:08:29.660
it's possible or rather was he saved by an

00:08:29.660 --> 00:08:32.570
impersonator who was protecting their

00:08:32.570 --> 00:08:33.550
reputation

00:08:34.460 --> 00:08:36.820
(Greirat) "now that we're both safe and sound

00:08:37.500 --> 00:08:39.560
thank the Gods for that

00:08:39.880 --> 00:08:42.600
I don't like cutting things so close.

00:08:42.600 --> 00:08:45.140
i might have died if it

00:08:45.149 --> 00:08:47.130
wasn't for that peculiar Onion Knight

00:08:48.360 --> 00:08:52.820
but in the end it all paid off

00:08:52.820 --> 00:08:55.820
take a good look, that's sure to be of

00:08:55.820 --> 00:08:58.040
some use

00:08:58.040 --> 00:09:01.220
you know I was thinking about leaving

00:09:01.220 --> 00:09:04.790
for another round of thieving there must

00:09:04.790 --> 00:09:07.250
be something of use in Lothric castle

00:09:08.440 --> 00:09:12.020
I'm aware of the danger, that castle is a

00:09:12.020 --> 00:09:13.310
deathtrap

00:09:13.310 --> 00:09:15.770
not a single man has returned from the

00:09:15.770 --> 00:09:18.940
castle unscathed, even back in the day...

00:09:20.380 --> 00:09:24.060
but I don't want to sit around and die a petty rat

00:09:25.260 --> 00:09:27.580
and I consider myself your friend"

00:09:29.300 --> 00:09:30.520
(Patches) "off to Lothric

00:09:31.120 --> 00:09:32.660
the Castle of no return

00:09:33.340 --> 00:09:36.840
That old thief's lost it if he thinks he has a chance in there

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:38.940
It's not like he's new to this game

00:09:38.940 --> 00:09:40.640
whats gotten in to him?"

00:09:40.649 --> 00:09:44.399
(Vaati) his debt repaid even Patches wouldn't

00:09:44.399 --> 00:09:46.379
risk Lothric for a friend...

00:09:46.440 --> 00:09:49.920
but Greirat well...he risks it for us

00:09:49.920 --> 00:09:52.820
self sacrifice it's in his character after all...

00:09:53.620 --> 00:09:55.619
but i don't think we're the only

00:09:55.619 --> 00:09:57.119
reason he goes

00:09:57.360 --> 00:09:58.740
think back to when he hid

00:09:58.740 --> 00:10:01.709
his grief over Loretta to how is so

00:10:01.709 --> 00:10:03.689
absorbed that he doesn't even notice you

00:10:03.689 --> 00:10:07.860
immediately after this dives into danger

00:10:07.860 --> 00:10:10.889
on your behalf his sorrow apparently

00:10:10.889 --> 00:10:15.119
forgotten and you think that's strange I

00:10:15.120 --> 00:10:17.680
don't think his sorrow is forgotten at all

00:10:18.260 --> 00:10:21.899
(Greirat) "I lived a petty rat, but would rather not

00:10:21.899 --> 00:10:23.959
die as one..."

00:10:25.120 --> 00:10:26.980
Greirat the thief

00:10:26.980 --> 00:10:28.079
a petty rat

00:10:28.079 --> 00:10:31.919
looking for an honorable escape

00:10:33.120 --> 00:10:35.960
Thank you Vaati for letting us add English subtitles. We had a blast! :)

